       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter one of these instead:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum labeled dose.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), which are common doses for pain or inflammation.\n\nDid you mean 1600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily? Or was 800 mg four times daily the intended dose? Tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If the patient needs more anti-inflammatory or analgesic effect than the maximum dose gives, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy or the prescriber about other options."
